---
layout: "home"
date: Last Modified
permalink: "/index.html"
localCSS: ["home", "making"]
---

{% from "macros/section-bar.njk" import sectionBar, listMore %}
{% from "macros/margin-list.njk" import entryRow, postRow, projectRow %}
{% from "macros/work-list.njk" import workList %}

{#
    Five practices on one frame. Every section is a bar and a list, every
    title starts on the main column's edge, and every fact about an entry —
    a date, a year, an organisation — sits beside it in the margin column.
    A section that leads somewhere ends on its way on, as the list's last
    line.

    WRITING, THINKING and MAKING read their own collections newest-first, so
    publishing is what changes this page. Nothing here is hand-ordered.

    WORKING comes last and reads src/_data/roles.js. It is the one section
    whose rows link nowhere, because no role has a page: the history is short
    enough to be the section rather than an index of one, and its last line
    sends anyone who wants the long form to LinkedIn.
#}
{% set essays = collections.writing | reverse | head(6) %}
{% set thoughts = collections.thinking | reverse | head(4) %}
{% set projects = collections.making | reverse | head(3) %}

<section class="hero">
    <p class="hero__statement">Sean Voisen is a software designer and engineer working to <strong>make computers better for human thinking &amp; creativity.</strong></p>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Writing") }}
    <ul class="margin-list">
    {%- for post in essays %}
    {{ postRow(post) }}
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {{ listMore("All essays", "/writing/") }}
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Thinking") }}
    <ul class="margin-list">
    {%- for post in thoughts %}
    {{ postRow(post) }}
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {{ listMore("All posts", "/thinking/") }}
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Making") }}
    <ul class="margin-list">
    {%- for project in projects %}
    {{ projectRow(project) }}
    {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {{ listMore("All projects", "/making/") }}
</section>

{# No way on: there is no "all reading" page to point at, and the Directory
   is already in the header. #}
<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Reading") }}
    <ul class="margin-list">
        {#- Summaries are the pages' Directory descriptions, so the two lists
            cannot describe a page differently. #}
        {{ entryRow("", "Bookshelf", navigation.items | getDescription("/bookshelf/"), "/bookshelf/") }}
        {{ entryRow("", "Philosophy for designers", navigation.items | getDescription("/philosophy-for-designers/"), "/philosophy-for-designers/") }}
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="home-section">
    {{ sectionBar("Working") }}
    {{ workList(roles) }}
    {{ listMore("Full work history on LinkedIn", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/svoisen/") }}
</section>
